# NIGHT SHIFT — GOODCO HQ.
#
# The brief: past midnight, every desk manned, the floor building spaceships in
# the dark. He is not looking for trouble; he kills everybody he ate lunch with
# because they are standing in a doorway, and never mentions it. So this is NOT
# a stealth cue — it is THE BUILDING'S OWN MUSIC, the loop THE GENUINELY GOOD
# COMPANY would put in its own lobby, still playing.
#
# THREE DECISIONS.
#
#   IT IS LOBBY MUSIC. Major sevenths, minor sevenths, a polite ii–V, a bright
#   advert of a B section. Played on cold pulses over a hard kit, at the tempo
#   of somebody walking to a meeting they are late for.
#
#   THE BUILDING IS SINKING. Bars 5–7 of the A section are bars 1–3 A SEMITONE
#   DOWN — the same shapes, the same tune, the whole floor a step lower than it
#   was four bars ago — and the dominant hauls it back up just in time to do it
#   again. The advert (B) does NOT sink: the pitch works, it is the workplace
#   underneath that does not.
#
#   THE PHOTOCOPIER. A dry mechanical clack every THREE sixteenths against a
#   bar of sixteen, so it lands somewhere new every bar and takes four to come
#   back round. It is in every single pattern including the breakdown, where it
#   is the only thing left. Nobody asked it to run all night.
#
# Compile:  node scripts/song-import.mjs content/songs/hq_lockdown.song --sheet

id     hq_lockdown
title  NIGHT SHIFT
tempo  128
about
  GOODCO's own lobby loop, still playing at one in the morning while the night
  shift is killed in the doorways. Major-seventh corporate warmth on cold
  pulses over a hard kit — and every four bars the floor SINKS: bars 5–7 are
  bars 1–3 a semitone down, the same tune played by a building that is a step
  lower than it was, with the dominant hauling it back up in time to do it
  again. The B section is the advert and does not sink, because the pitch
  works fine; it is the workplace under it that does not. Through all of it a
  photocopier clacks every three sixteenths against a bar of sixteen, landing
  somewhere new every bar, alone in the breakdown. Original melodies; nothing
  sampled.

# ── THE CAST ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The voice on the tannoy: a detuned square, polite, slightly too bright.
voice lead   square vol=.028 gate=.8 detune=7 echo=.22 vib=5/10/220
# The lobby piano — seventh-chord stabs on the off-beat, thin and out of tune.
voice keys   square vol=.013 gate=.25 detune=10 pan=.3 echo=.18
# The strip lights: a lowpassed saw chugging sixteenths. Not a bass, a HUM.
voice strip  saw vol=.0095 gate=.4 lp=1800 pan=-0.3
# The floor.
voice bass   triangle vol=.055 gate=.8

# ── THE KIT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
drum kick    triangle vol=.06 gate=1 slide=.25 note=D2
drum snare   noise vol=.033 gate=.7 hp=1400
drum hat     noise vol=.0105 gate=.25 hp=6800 pan=.25
# THE PHOTOCOPIER — every third sixteenth, four bars to come back round.
drum copier  noise vol=.017 gate=.06 bp=2600 pan=-0.45

# ── INTRO — a lift, a corridor, and something already running ───────────────
section intro
  chords Dm7 | Dm7 | A7 | A7
  copier x..x..x..x..x..x|..x..x..x..x..x.|.x..x..x..x..x..|x..x..x..x..x..x
  strip  .*16 | .*16 | chug:4 | chug:4
  bass   .*16 | .*16 | four:2 | four:2
  keys   .*16 | .*16 | .*16 | offbeat:4
  hat    ................|................|..x...x...x...x.|..x...x...x...x.

# ── A — the vamp, and the floor going out from under it halfway through ─────
section a
  chords Dm7 | Gm7 | Bbmaj7 | A7 | C#m7 | F#m7 | Amaj7 | A7
  lead   a4*2 d5*2 f5*4 e5*4 d5*4 | a#4*4 d5*4 f5*8 | d5*4 f5*2 a5*2 g5*8 | e5*4 c#5*4 a4*8
         g#4*2 c#5*2 e5*4 d#5*4 c#5*4 | a4*4 c#5*4 e5*8 | c#5*4 e5*2 g#5*2 f#5*8 | g5*4 e5*4 a4*8
  keys   offbeat 4
  strip  chug 4
  bass   pump 2
  kick   x.....x.x.......|x.......x...x...
  snare  ....x.......x...
  hat    ..x...x...x...x.
  copier x..x..x..x..x..x|..x..x..x..x..x.|.x..x..x..x..x..|x..x..x..x..x..x

# ── B — THE ADVERT. It is in a major key, it is sincere, and it works ───────
section b
  chords Fmaj7 | Dm7 | Bbmaj7 | C | Fmaj7 | Dm7 | Gm7 | A7
  lead   f5*4 a5*4 c6*8 | a5*4 f5*4 d5*8 | d5*4 f5*4 a5*8 | g5*8 e5*8
         f5*4 a5*4 c6*4 d6*4 | c6*8 a5*8 | a#5*4 a5*4 g5*8 | e5*4 c#5*4 a4*8
  keys   offbeat 4
  strip  chug 4
  bass   pump 2
  kick   x.....x.x.......|x.......x...x...
  snare  ....x.......x...
  hat    x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.
  copier x..x..x..x..x..x|..x..x..x..x..x.|.x..x..x..x..x..|x..x..x..x..x..x

# ── BREAK — everybody has gone home except the machine that has not ─────────
section break
  chords Dm7 | Dm7 | C#m7 | C#m7 | Dm7 | Dm7 | A7 | A7
  keys   arp16 4
  bass   d2*8 .*8 | .*16 | c#2*8 .*8 | .*16
         d2*8 .*8 | .*16 | a2*8 .*8 | a2*8 e3*8
  copier x..x..x..x..x..x|..x..x..x..x..x.|.x..x..x..x..x..|x..x..x..x..x..x

# ── BUILD — the stairwell. A chromatic climb nobody can walk off ───────────
section build
  chords Dm | D#dim | Em | F | F#dim | Gm | G#dim | A
  strip  chug 4
  keys   offbeat 4
  bass   pump 2
  lead   d5*16 | d#5*16 | e5*16 | f5*16
         f#5*16 | g5*16 | g#5*8 a5*8 | a5*4 c#6*4 e6*8
  kick   x.......x.......
  snare  ....x.......x...|....x.......x...|....x.......x.x.|....x.......x.x.
         ....x...x.x.x.x.|....x...x.x.x.x.|x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.|xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
  hat    x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.
  copier x..x..x..x..x..x|..x..x..x..x..x.|.x..x..x..x..x..|x..x..x..x..x..x

# ── TURN — the vamp again, wider, and it still will not land ───────────────
section turn
  chords Dm7 | Gm7 | Bbmaj7 | A7 | C#m7 | F#m7 | Amaj7 | A7
  lead   d6*4 c6*4 a5*8 | a#5*8 g5*8 | f5*4 a5*4 d6*8 | c#6*4 a5*4 e5*8
         c#6*4 b5*4 g#5*8 | a5*8 f#5*8 | e5*4 g#5*4 c#6*8 | c#6*4 a5*4 e5*8
  keys   stab 4
  strip  chug 4
  bass   gallop 2
  kick   x.....x.x.......|x.......x...x...
  snare  ....x.......x...|....x.......x.x.
  hat    x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.
  copier x..x..x..x..x..x|..x..x..x..x..x.|.x..x..x..x..x..|x..x..x..x..x..x

order  intro a b a break build b turn
